1. Definition of Abstract Class

An Abstract Class is a class that contains at least one pure virtual function.
It cannot be instantiated directly.
It is mainly used as a base class for derived classes.
It provides a common structure or interface to derived classes.

Abstract Class ऐसी class होती है जिसमें कम-से-कम एक pure virtual function होता है।
इसका direct object नहीं बनाया जा सकता।
इसका मुख्य उपयोग base class के रूप में किया जाता है।
यह derived classes को common structure या interface प्रदान करती है।
Easy Example
class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

यहाँ Animal एक Abstract Class है।

    2. Pure Virtual Function

        A Pure Virtual Function is a virtual function declared with = 0. It does not provide a required implementation in the base class.Derived classes are expected to override it.

                                                                      Pure Virtual Function वह virtual function है जिसे = 0 के साथ declare किया जाता है।
            Base class में इसका implementation आवश्यक नहीं होता।
                Derived class को इसे override करना पड़ता है।

                    Syntax virtual void
                    display() = 0;
Example class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};
3. Syntax of Abstract Class
    English class ClassName
{
public:
    virtual returnType functionName() = 0;
};

Abstract class बनाने के लिए class के अंदर कम - से - कम एक pure virtual function declare किया जाता है।

                                                   Example class Shape
{
public:
    virtual void draw() = 0;
};

4. Why Abstract Class is Used?

Abstract classes are used to:

Provide a common interface.
Define common rules for derived classes.
Achieve abstraction.
Support runtime polymorphism.
Avoid creating objects of an incomplete/general base concept.

Abstract class का उपयोग:

Common interface देने के लिए।
Derived classes के लिए common rules बनाने के लिए।
Abstraction प्राप्त करने के लिए।
Runtime polymorphism support करने के लिए।
General/base concept का direct object बनने से रोकने के लिए।

5. Object of Abstract Class

An object of an abstract class cannot be created directly.
This is because the class contains at least one pure virtual function.

Abstract class का direct object नहीं बनाया जा सकता।
इसका कारण है कि इसमें कम-से-कम एक pure virtual function होता है।
Example
class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

int main()
{
    Animal a; //  Error
}
याद रखें
        Abstract Class
      ↓ Direct Object

    6. Pointer /
    Reference to Abstract Class

        Although an abstract class cannot have a direct object,
    its pointer or reference can be created.The pointer / reference can refer to an object of a derived class.

                                                          Abstract class का direct object नहीं बना सकते। लेकिन उसका pointer या reference बनाया जा सकता है। यह pointer /
                       reference derived class के object को refer कर सकता है।
                           Example class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

class Dog : public Animal
{
public:
    void sound()
    {
        cout << "Dog barks";
    }
};

int main()
{
    Dog d;

    Animal *ptr = &d;

    ptr->sound();
}

Output:

Dog barks

7. Derived Class

A class derived from an abstract class must provide implementations for all inherited pure virtual functions to become a concrete class.
After implementing them, its object can be created.

Abstract class से derived class बनाने पर inherited pure virtual functions को implement/override करना पड़ता है।
सभी required pure virtual functions को override करने के बाद derived class का object बनाया जा सकता है।
Example
class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

class Dog : public Animal
{
public:
    void sound()
    {
        cout << "Dog barks";
    }
};

अब :

    Dog d;

Valid है।

    8. Overriding Pure Virtual Function

        The derived class should override the pure virtual function.This provides the actual implementation of the function.

    Derived class को pure virtual function को override करना चाहिए।
        इससे function का actual implementation मिलता है।
            Example class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

class Dog : public Animal
{
public:
    void sound() override
    {
        cout << "Dog barks";
    }
};

यहाँ :

    void
    sound() override

    ने base class के pure virtual function को implement किया।

    9. Multiple Pure Virtual Functions

    An abstract class can contain multiple pure virtual functions.The derived class must implement all of them to become concrete.

    एक abstract class में multiple pure virtual functions हो सकते हैं।
    Derived class को सभी required functions implement करने पड़ते हैं।
    Example
    class Shape
{
public:
    virtual void draw() = 0;
    virtual void area() = 0;
};

class Circle : public Shape
{
public:
    void draw() override
    {
        cout << "Drawing Circle" << endl;
    }

    void area() override
    {
        cout << "Area of Circle" << endl;
    }
};

10. Constructor in Abstract Class

    An abstract class can have a constructor.Its constructor is called when a derived class object is created.The abstract class itself still cannot be instantiated directly.

    Abstract class में constructor हो सकता है।
        Derived class का object बनाते समय base abstract class का constructor call होता है।
            फिर भी abstract class का direct object नहीं बनाया जा सकता।
                Example class Animal
{
public:
    Animal()
    {
        cout << "Animal Constructor" << endl;
    }

    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

class Dog : public Animal
{
public:
    void sound() override
    {
        cout << "Dog Barks" << endl;
    }
};

जब :

    Dog d;

होगा :

    Animal Constructor
        ↓ Dog Object Created

    11. Destructor in Abstract Class

        An abstract class can have a destructor.A virtual destructor is especially useful when deleting derived objects through a base -
    class pointer.

    Abstract class में destructor हो सकता है।
        Base class pointer से derived object delete करने की situation में virtual destructor important होता है।
            Example class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;

    virtual ~Animal()
    {
        cout << "Animal Destructor";
    }
};

12. Normal Functions in Abstract Class

An abstract class can contain normal member functions.
It is not necessary for every function to be pure virtual.

Abstract class में normal member functions भी हो सकते हैं।
ऐसा जरूरी नहीं है कि class के सभी functions pure virtual हों।
Example
class Animal
{
public:
    void eat()
    {
        cout << "Animal eats" << endl;
    }

    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

यहाँ :

    eat()    → Normal Function
    sound()  → Pure Virtual Function

    इसलिए Animal abstract class है।

    13. Data Members in Abstract Class

    An abstract class can contain data members like a normal class.Derived classes can access them according to their access specifier.

    Abstract class में normal variables
    / data members हो सकते हैं।
    Derived class उन्हें access कर सकती है,
    depending on access specifier।
    Example
    class Animal
{
public:
    string name;

    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

14. Abstract Class with Multiple Derived Classes

    One abstract class can have multiple derived classes,
    and each derived class can provide its own implementation.

        एक abstract class से कई derived classes बनाई जा सकती हैं और प्रत्येक derived class अपने तरीके से pure virtual function implement कर सकती है।

            Example
                Animal |
        ┌───────┴───────┐
        ↓               ↓ Dog Cat
        ↓               ↓ Dog barks Cat meows

            Code :

    class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

class Dog : public Animal
{
public:
    void sound() override
    {
        cout << "Dog barks";
    }
};

class Cat : public Animal
{
public:
    void sound() override
    {
        cout << "Cat meows";
    }
};

15. Runtime Polymorphism with Abstract Class

        Abstract classes can be used with base -
    class pointers / references to achieve runtime polymorphism.Abstract class के pointer / reference का उपयोग करके runtime polymorphism प्राप्त किया जा सकता है।

                                                                                               Example Animal *ptr;

Dog d;
Cat c;

ptr = &d;
ptr->sound();

ptr = &c;
ptr->sound();

Output : Dog barks
             Cat meows

         16. If Derived Class Does Not Override

             If a derived class does not implement all inherited pure virtual functions,
         it also remains an abstract class.

         अगर derived class सभी inherited pure virtual functions को override नहीं करती,
         तो वह भी abstract class बनी रहती है।

             Example class Animal
{
public:
    virtual void sound() = 0;
};

class Dog : public Animal
{
    // sound() not implemented
};

अब :

    Dog d; //  Error

क्योंकि Dog अभी भी abstract है।

21. Advantages of Abstract Class

Provides abstraction.
Provides a common interface.
Supports code reusability.
Supports runtime polymorphism.
Provides a common structure for derived classes.
Prevents direct creation of inappropriate/general base objects.

Abstraction प्रदान करती है।
Common interface प्रदान करती है।
Code reusability में मदद करती है।
Runtime polymorphism support करती है।
Derived classes को common structure देती है।
General base class के unwanted direct objects को रोकती है।

22. Disadvantages / Limitations

Cannot create a direct object.
Derived classes must implement required pure virtual functions.
Improper design can make inheritance unnecessarily complex.
Virtual functions may involve runtime dispatch overhead.

इसका direct object नहीं बना सकते।
Derived class को required pure virtual functions implement करने पड़ते हैं।
गलत design से inheritance complex हो सकती है।
Virtual function के कारण runtime dispatch का थोड़ा overhead हो सकता है।

Characteristics of Abstract Class in C++ 

• Cannot be Instantiated
 An abstract class cannot be instantiated directly.
 Abstract class का direct object नहीं बनाया जा सकता।
Example: Animal obj;

• Contains Pure Virtual Function
        An abstract class contains at least one pure virtual function.Abstract class में कम -
    से - कम एक pure virtual function होता है। Example : virtual void sound() = 0;

• Used as a Base Class
 An abstract class is mainly used as a base class for derived classes.
 Abstract class का मुख्य रूप से derived classes की base class के रूप में उपयोग किया जाता है।

• Supports Abstraction
 It helps hide unnecessary implementation details and shows only the required features.
 यह unnecessary implementation details को hide करके केवल required features को दिखाने में मदद करती है।

• Supports Polymorphism
 It supports runtime polymorphism through base-class pointers or references.
 यह base-class pointer या reference के माध्यम से runtime polymorphism को support करती है।

• Can Have Normal Functions
 An abstract class can contain normal member functions along with pure virtual functions.
 Abstract class में pure virtual functions के साथ normal member functions भी हो सकते हैं।

• Can Have Data Members
 An abstract class can contain data members or variables.
 Abstract class में data members या variables भी हो सकते हैं।

• Can Have Constructor
 An abstract class can have a constructor, which is called when a derived-class object is created.
 Abstract class में constructor हो सकता है, जो derived-class का object बनाते समय call होता है।

• Can Have Destructor
 An abstract class can have a destructor, and a virtual destructor is useful when deleting derived objects through a base pointer.
 Abstract class में destructor हो सकता है और base pointer के द्वारा derived object को delete करते समय virtual destructor useful होता है।

• Can Have Multiple Pure Virtual Functions
 An abstract class can contain more than one pure virtual function.
 Abstract class में एक से अधिक pure virtual functions हो सकते हैं।

• Derived Class Must Implement Pure Virtual Functions
 A derived class must override all required pure virtual functions to become a concrete class.
 Derived class को concrete class बनने के लिए सभी required pure virtual functions को override करना पड़ता है।

• Pointer and Reference are Allowed
 A pointer or reference to an abstract class can be created, but its direct object cannot be created.
 Abstract class का pointer या reference बनाया जा सकता है, लेकिन इसका direct object नहीं बनाया जा सकता।

• Derived Class Object Can Be Created
 An object of a derived class can be created if it implements all inherited pure virtual functions.
 अगर derived class सभी inherited pure virtual functions को implement कर देती है, तो उसका object बनाया जा सकता है।

• Provides Common Interface
 An abstract class provides a common interface or common rules for derived classes.
 Abstract class derived classes के लिए common interface या common rules प्रदान करती है।


